Experimental Process
At first, participants were informed with the experimental procedure and content. After wearing the eye tracker and completing the calibration process, the experiment began with the random presentation of Task 1 or Task 2. The eye tracker recorded the participants’ the first fixation time in different areas. After completing the experiment, participants were required to fill out the SART questionnaire (see Figure 3).
Task 1: The vehicle initially drived at the speed of 70 km/h. Participants were required to adjust their speed promptly based on the speed limit

